    <p>To anyone outside the travel industry, the screen of a Global Distribution System (GDS) looks exactly like the source code from a science fiction movie. Letters, numbers, slashes, and commands are grouped in dense blocks of information. However, for tourism professionals, that cryptic text is the universal language of business. At the heart of all that data lies the <strong>PNR</strong>, the single most vital element of any travel reservation.</p>

